---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';
import type { Product } from '../../data/products';

const slugOrder = [
  'generac-22kw-guardian',
  'kohler-20rescl-20kw',
  'briggs-stratton-10kw-standby',
];

const picks = slugOrder.map(slug => products.find(p => p.slug === slug)!).filter(Boolean) as Product[];
const topPick = picks[0];

const bestFor: Record<string, string> = {
  'generac-22kw-guardian':      'Best Overall — Most Trusted, Covers Up to 4,000 Sq Ft',
  'kohler-20rescl-20kw':        'Best Premium — Quietest Operation, Commercial-Grade Engine',
  'briggs-stratton-10kw-standby':'Best Budget — Essential Circuits in Large Homes',
};

const homeSizeFit: Record<string, string> = {
  'generac-22kw-guardian':      '2,500–4,500+ sq ft with central A/C',
  'kohler-20rescl-20kw':        '2,000–4,000 sq ft with central A/C',
  'briggs-stratton-10kw-standby':'Any size — essential circuits only (no central A/C)',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Best Whole Home Generator for Large Homes (2025) — 3,000–5,000+ Sq Ft Coverage"
  description="The best whole home standby generators for large homes in 2025. Generac 22kW vs Kohler 20kW vs Briggs & Stratton 10kW — which handles a 3,000+ square foot home with multiple A/C units."
>
  <div class="bg-amber-50 border-b border-amber-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-2 text-xs text-amber-800 text-center">
      This site earns commissions from purchases made through our links at no extra cost to you.
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">

    <nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-green-700">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">›</span>
      <a href="/backup-power/" class="hover:text-green-700">Backup Power</a>
      <span class="mx-2">›</span>
      Best Whole Home Generator for Large Homes
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 leading-tight">
      Best Whole Home Generator for Large Homes (2025)
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-6">Last updated: June 2025 · 3,000–5,000+ sq ft</p>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      Large homes — 3,000 to 5,000+ square feet — place different demands on a standby generator than standard 2,000 sq ft homes. Multiple HVAC zones, multiple refrigerators, electric water heaters, and larger electrical panels mean you need real kilowatt capacity, not the entry-level 10kW units that work for smaller homes.
    </p>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      The 20–22kW standby generators from Generac and Kohler are the right tools for the job. They run the whole house — all circuits, all A/C zones, all appliances — without load management or manual circuit selection. For homeowners who want to run only essential circuits and save on installation, the Briggs & Stratton 10kW is the budget entry point, with the honest caveat that it won't run central A/C.
    </p>

    <!-- Load Calculator Box -->
    <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-2xl p-5 mb-8">
      <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-sm">Typical electrical loads in a large home:</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-xs border-collapse">
          <thead class="bg-blue-100">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-2 py-1.5 text-left border border-blue-200">Appliance</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-1.5 text-left border border-blue-200">Running Load</th>
              <th class="px-2 py-1.5 text-left border border-blue-200">Surge</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">Central A/C (5-ton / 5,000 sq ft)</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">6,000W</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">18,000W+</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-blue-50"><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">Central A/C zone 2 (3-ton)</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">3,500W</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">11,000W</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">Electric oven/range</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">6,000W</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">6,000W</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-blue-50"><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">Electric dryer</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">5,000W</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">6,500W</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">Refrigerator × 2</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">400–600W</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200">2,000W+</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-blue-50"><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200 font-medium">Lights + outlets + misc.</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200 font-medium">2,000–4,000W</td><td class="px-2 py-1 border border-blue-200 font-medium">—</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-blue-800 mt-3">A 22kW generator handles all of this running simultaneously. A 10kW handles only the last row (lights, outlets, misc).</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Top Pick -->
    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Top Pick for Large Homes</p>
      <p class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{topPick.name}</p>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2">{topPick.tagline}</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-3">Fits: {homeSizeFit[topPick.slug]}</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-700">${topPick.price}</span>
        <a href={topPick.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"
           class="bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-md text-sm transition-colors">
          View on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Comparison Table -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Quick Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-200">
        <thead class="bg-gray-100">
          <tr>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Generator</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Best For</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Output</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Home Size Fit</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Unit Price</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Link</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {picks.map((p, i) => (
            <tr class={i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-gray-50'}>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 font-medium">{p.name}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-green-700 font-medium">{bestFor[p.slug]}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">{p.specs['Output']}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-xs">{homeSizeFit[p.slug]}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">${p.price}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">
                <a href={p.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"
                   class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">Amazon →</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-2xl p-5 mb-10 text-sm text-yellow-900">
      <strong>Total installed cost reminder:</strong> Generator unit price is only part of the total. Installation — which requires a licensed electrician — adds $3,000–6,000. Include permits, a concrete pad, and transfer switch (if not included) and budget $7,000–13,000 total for a 20–22kW system in a large home. Get three quotes from licensed installers in your area.
    </div>

    <!-- Reviews -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Full Reviews</h2>

    {picks.map((p, i) => (
      <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">
              #{i + 1} — {bestFor[p.slug]}
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">{p.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1">{p.tagline}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-right flex-shrink-0">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-700">${p.price}</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-0.5">{p.specs['Output']}</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm mb-4">
          {Object.entries(p.specs).map(([key, val]) => (
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded px-3 py-1.5">
              <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">{key}:</span> {val}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-green-700 mb-1 text-sm">Pros</div>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              {p.pros.map(pro => <li class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="text-green-500 mt-0.5">✓</span><span>{pro}</span></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-red-600 mb-1 text-sm">Cons</div>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              {p.cons.map(con => <li class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="text-red-400 mt-0.5">✗</span><span>{con}</span></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a href={p.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"
           class="inline-block bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-md text-sm transition-colors">
          Check Price on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>
    ))}

    <!-- Buying Guide -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Large Home Generator Buying Guide</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Why Large Homes Need 20kW+</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        The critical load in large homes is multi-zone air conditioning. A 5,000 sq ft home in a hot climate may have two 3–5-ton A/C units. Each 3-ton unit draws 3,500W running, with a 10,000W+ starting surge. When both kick on at the same time, you need a generator that can handle that combined surge. A 22kW generator with a 27.5kVA surge rating handles even worst-case simultaneous starts without browning out.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Natural Gas vs. Propane for Large Homes</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        Both Generac and Kohler run on natural gas or propane. Natural gas is the preferred fuel if you have a gas line — it runs indefinitely without refueling. Propane requires a large tank (500–1,000 gallon) for extended outages; at 22kW output, a propane generator burns roughly 2–3 gallons per hour. For a large home with a multi-day outage risk, a natural gas hookup is worth the installation cost.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Do Very Large Homes Need More Than 22kW?</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
        For homes above 5,000 sq ft with electric heating or multiple large HVAC systems, a liquid-cooled generator in the 30–48kW range may be appropriate. These units are sold exclusively through Generac and Kohler dealers, not on Amazon, and require professional load calculation before sizing. If your electrical panel is 400A (not the standard 200A), consult a licensed generator installer — you may need a larger unit than what's available retail.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Internal Links -->
    <div class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Related Guides</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/best-whole-home-generator-2000-sq-ft/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Whole Home Generator for 2,000 Sq Ft Homes</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/generac-vs-kohler/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Generac vs Kohler — Detailed Comparison</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/best-whole-home-generator-brands-compared/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Whole Home Generator Brands Compared</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/what-size-generator-do-i-need/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">What Size Generator Do I Need?</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/how-to-choose-a-whole-home-generator/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Choose a Whole Home Generator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </article>
</Layout>
